{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You were brought in after being confused in clinic and having trouble standing. Can you tell me how you're feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling a bit better. My head is clearer now. I was so weak earlier—I couldn’t even get up from the toilet without help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your team mentioned that. You also had a high calcium level—11.2—which can cause confusion and weakness. You got fluids and a medication called pamidronate before coming in. That should help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. That makes sense. I’ve had high calcium before with my myeloma. But I’ve also been gasping for air when I walk. Is that from the myeloma too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be related. We’re checking things now. You had a chest X-ray, and it showed some fluid buildup around the heart, but no pneumonia. We’ll do more tests to be sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:21:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see. And my back pain—it’s been worse lately. Do you think the myeloma is getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a concern. Your oncologist thinks the myeloma may be progressing. You already started a 4-day course of high-dose dexamethasone today to help control it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:24:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Dexamethasone? That’s a steroid, right? I’ve had it before. It messes with my blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:25:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And your blood sugar was already high—234. With steroids, it could go even higher. We’ll monitor it closely and adjust your insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:26:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on insulin at home, but I don’t like the sliding scale. It’s hard to keep up with."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have the diabetes team see you tomorrow to help fine-tune it. For now, we’ll start a temporary insulin drip to keep things stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:29:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. And my blood pressure’s been high too. My doctor keeps changing my meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:30:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s 150/80 now, and steroids can make it worse. We’ll adjust your blood pressure meds while you’re here. You’re on diltiazem and carvedilol—those will stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:31:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. I just want to get back on track. I’m worried about falling again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-11-10 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure you’re safe. Please don’t get up without calling for help, especially with your IV. We’ll help you to the bathroom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-11-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood work from last night shows your calcium is coming down to 9.6. That’s great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-11-11 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my kidney numbers? Last time I was in, my creatinine was high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-11-11 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s 1.7 now, which is elevated from your baseline. We think it’s due to dehydration, high calcium, and the myeloma. With fluids and treatment, it should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-11-11 08:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood sugar? I checked it last night before bed—it was 280."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-11-11 08:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the steroid is pushing it up. The endocrinology team will see you today. They might increase your long-acting insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-11-11 08:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I just hope I don’t have another episode like last time with the insulin drip."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-11-11 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor closely. Your blood cultures came back clean—no infection, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-11-11 08:09:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had C. diff before, so I’m still on oral vancomycin. Should I keep taking it every day?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-11-11 08:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on it daily in the hospital, but normally you take it every 72 hours. We’ll switch you back before discharge unless your GI doctor says otherwise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-11-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a VQ scan yesterday to check for blood clots in your lungs. It came back normal—no pulmonary embolism."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-11-12 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s a relief. I was worried because of my history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-11-12 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ve had PEs before. But this time, your shortness of breath is likely from anemia. Your hemoglobin is 8.5, so we’re giving you one unit of red blood cells today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-11-12 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help me feel stronger?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-11-12 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should. You’ll likely notice more energy and less breathlessness in the next day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-11-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin is up to 9.1 after the transfusion. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-11-13 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I walked to the bathroom with help and didn’t feel as winded."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-11-13 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. Your myeloma team has also started you on a new regimen: dexamethasone, Velcade, and Cytoxan, because daratumumab wasn’t working anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-11-13 10:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember Cytoxan. It’s strong. Any side effects I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-11-13 10:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll watch your blood counts closely. It can lower your white cells and platelets. You might feel more tired, but we’ll support you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-11-14 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is down to 1.5 today—still a bit high, but improving. Your kidneys are responding to treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-11-14 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My blood sugar was 310 this morning, though. Is that normal with the steroid?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-11-14 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Unfortunately, yes. The endocrinology team increased your glargine insulin to 25 units at bedtime. They also added a sliding scale for corrections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-11-14 08:34:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need to keep doing that at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-11-14 08:35:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, yes. You’ll follow up with your endocrinologist after discharge. If you get steroids again, they may need to help manage it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-11-15 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has been running high—around 160/90. We’ve increased your diltiazem from 240 to 360 mg daily and added amlodipine 5 mg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-11-15 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on so many BP meds. Will I stay on all of them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-11-15 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see how it goes. You should follow up with your cardiologist to adjust them as needed. The steroids are making it harder to control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-11-16 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your myeloma treatment is going well. You got your Velcade dose yesterday through your port. Any numbness or tingling in your feet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-11-16 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just the usual—my neuropathy is always there. But it hasn’t gotten worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-11-16 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’re monitoring that. Your platelets are a bit low—47—so we’ll watch for bruising or bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-11-17 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re getting your Cytoxan infusion now through your peripheral line. It’ll take a few hours. We’ll keep an eye on your vitals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-11-17 12:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I feel fine so far. Any nausea I should expect?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2176-11-17 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve given you ondansetron to prevent that. Let us know if you feel sick or dizzy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2176-11-18 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning show your calcium is stable at 9.6, creatinine is 1.4, and you’re still anemic at 7.5. But you’re feeling well, so we’re planning for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2176-11-18 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my medications? So many changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2176-11-18 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve updated them. Your diltiazem is now 360 mg, you’re on amlodipine 5 mg daily, and your insulin is 25 units glargine at bedtime with sliding scale."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2176-11-18 08:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the vancomycin for C. diff?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2176-11-18 08:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go back to taking it every 72 hours unless your GI doctor advises otherwise. We’ll include that in your discharge instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2176-11-18 08:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I see my eye doctor? My eyes have been itchy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2176-11-18 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your oncologist mentioned moderate episcleritis. We recommend an ophthalmology follow-up. I’ll add a referral."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2176-11-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge tomorrow. Your condition is stable: clear thinking, better strength, and labs are improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2176-11-19 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2176-11-19 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Check your blood sugar before meals and at bedtime. If it’s below 100 or above 300, call your endocrinologist. Watch for dizziness, shortness of breath, or confusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2176-11-19 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my back pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2176-11-19 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue your oxycodone as needed. But if the pain worsens suddenly, get checked—could be a bone issue from myeloma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2176-11-19 09:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2176-11-19 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll send all your records to your doctors. Please follow up with oncology, endocrinology, and your cardiologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Your wife is here, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, she’s in the waiting room. I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Here’s your discharge summary and prescriptions. Take it easy for a few days and keep all your follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for helping me feel like myself again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I restart my regular myeloma meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your oncologist will guide you on the new regimen: dexamethasone, Velcade, and Cytoxan. They’ll schedule your next dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:09:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll call them today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. And call us if anything changes before your appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:11:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:14:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:16:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:19:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ll be there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:21:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, doc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will help you get dressed and discharged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:24:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:25:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:26:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2176-11-20 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-11-10 19:58:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-11-20 18:18:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted with altered mental status and weakness due to hypercalcemia in the setting of relapsed refractory multiple myeloma. He received pamidronate in clinic prior to admission, which resolved his hypercalcemia. During his stay, he was treated with a 4-day pulse of dexamethasone followed by a new regimen of dexamethasone, Velcade, and Cytoxan due to progression of myeloma. His hospital course was complicated by steroid-induced hyperglycemia requiring insulin drip and dose adjustments, and poorly controlled hypertension managed with increased diltiazem and addition of amlodipine. Acute kidney injury, likely from hypercalcemia and dehydration, improved from a creatinine of 1.7 to 1.3. Dyspnea was attributed to anemia, and he was transfused one unit of red blood cells with symptom improvement. He remained on oral vancomycin for C. diff prevention and was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up planned in oncology, endocrinology, and cardiology.",
    "problems": [
      "Multiple myeloma in relapse",
      "Hypercalcemia",
      "Acute kidney injury",
      "Altered mental status",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with hyperglycemia",
      "Hypertension",
      "Dyspnea",
      "Anemia",
      "History of C. diff infection",
      "Peripheral neuropathy",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea",
      "Chronic kidney disease",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism"
    ]
  }
}
